          "text": "1"
        }
      ],
      "marks": null,
      "negativeMarks": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "C",
      "correctText": "$-2\\log_e 5$",
      "explanation": "Multiply numerator and denominator by \\(\\sqrt{x^2-x+1}+1\\). The expression becomes\n\\[\n\\lim_{x\\to0}\\frac{5^x-1}{x}\\cdot\n\\frac{\\sqrt{x^2-x+1}+1}{x-1}.\n\\]\nHence the value is\n\\[\n\\log_e5\\cdot\\frac{2}{-1}=-2\\log_e5.\n\\]\nChoice (C).",
