    "question": {
      "pdfName": "Engineering_mathematics_2.pdf",
      "text": "If\n\\[\nf(x)=\n\\begin{cases}\nx^2+5x-13,&x<1,\\\\\nx-8,&x\\ge1,\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\nthen \\(\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to1}f(x)=\\)",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "−8"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "−7"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "7"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "does not exist"
        }
      ],
      "marks": null,
      "negativeMarks": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "B",
      "correctText": "−7",
      "explanation": "We know\n\\[\n\\lim_{x\\to1}f(x)=\\lim_{x\\to1^-}f(x)=\\lim_{x\\to1^+}f(x).\n\\]\nThe left-hand limit is\n\\[\n\\lim_{x\\to1^-}(x^2+5x-13)=-7,\n\\]\nand the right-hand limit is\n\\[\n\\lim_{x\\to1^+}(x-8)=-7.\n\\]\nTherefore \\(\\lim_{x\\to1}f(x)=-7\\). Choice (B).",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
    "classification": {
      "subject": "Engineering Mathematics",
      "topic": "Limits and continuity",
