      "difficulty": null
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "A",
      "correctText": "0",
      "explanation": "Write\n\\[\nf(x)=a([x]-5)+b([x]+5).\n\\]\nFor \\(x\\to5^-\\),\n\\[\n\\lim_{x\\to5^-}f(x)=-a+9b.\n\\]\nFor \\(x\\to5^+\\),\n\\[\n\\lim_{x\\to5^+}f(x)=10b.\n\\]\nContinuity at \\(x=5\\) gives \\(-a+9b=10b\\), hence \\(a+b=0\\). Choice (A).",
