    "question": {
      "pdfName": "Engineering_mathematics_2.pdf",
      "text": "If \\(y=ax^2+3\\log x+bx\\) has its extreme value at \\(x=1\\) and \\(x=-1\\), then the value of \\(2a-b\\) is",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "3"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "0"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "−1"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "−3"
        }
      ],
      "marks": null,
      "negativeMarks": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "D",
      "correctText": "−3",
      "explanation": "Let \\(f(x)=ax^2+3\\log x+bx\\). Then\n\\[\nf'(x)=2ax+\\frac3x+b.\n\\]\nGiven that \\(f(x)\\) has extreme values at \\(x=-1\\) and \\(x=1\\), \\(f'(-1)=0\\) and \\(f'(1)=0\\). From \\(f'(-1)=0\\),\n\\[\n-2a+b=3,\n\\]\nso\n\\[\n2a-b=-3.\n\\]\nChoice (D).",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
