      "correctOption": "C",
      "correctText": "$-\\frac23$",
      "explanation": "Given \\(f(x)=x(x+2)(x-1)\\), it is continuous on \\([-1,0]\\) and differentiable on \\((-1,0)\\). Here \\(a=-1,\\ b=0\\),\n\\[\nf(b)=0,\\qquad f(a)=(-1)(1)(-2)=2,\n\\]\nand\n\\[\nf'(x)=3x^2+2x-2.\n\\]\nBy Lagrange's mean value theorem,\n\\[\nf'(c)=\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}=\\frac{0-2}{1}=-2.\n\\]\nHence\n\\[\n3c^2+2c-2=-2\\Rightarrow3c^2+2c=0.\n\\]\nThus \\(c=0\\) or \\(c=-\\frac23\\). Since \\(c\\in(-1,0)\\),\n\\[\nc=-\\frac23.\n\\]\nChoice (C).",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
