          "text": "$\\sin2u$"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "$2\\cos2u$"
        }
      ],
      "marks": null,
      "negativeMarks": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "C",
      "correctText": "$\\sin2u$",
      "explanation": "Let\n\\[\n\\tan u=\\frac{x^3-y^3}{x+y}.\n\\]\nThis is a homogeneous function of degree \\(2\\). By Euler's theorem,\n\\[\nx\\frac{\\partial(\\tan u)}{\\partial x}\n+y\\frac{\\partial(\\tan u)}{\\partial y}=2\\tan u.\n\\]\nSince\n\\[\n\\frac{\\partial(\\tan u)}{\\partial x}=\\sec^2u\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x},\n\\qquad\n\\frac{\\partial(\\tan u)}{\\partial y}=\\sec^2u\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y},\n\\]\nwe get\n\\[\nx\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x}+y\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y}\n=\\frac{2\\tan u}{\\sec^2u}\n=2\\sin u\\cos u\n=\\sin2u.\n\\]\nChoice (C).",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
    "classification": {
      "subject": "Engineering Mathematics",
      "topic": "Euler's theorem for homogeneous functions",
      "subtopic": null,
